\caption(All eleven original frequent sets survive. Beer and diapers intersect at rows 4,5,6; the triple uses two conditional pair operands, rather than an original singleton.)
\alttext(A native bar plot shows singleton supports of five for bread and milk, four for butter and beer, and three for diapers.)

The triple's operands are {bread,milk} and {bread,butter}, sharing the
bread prefix. Intersecting their tids gives rows {0,3,7}, support three.
These are actual operands recorded by the run. A trace built instead by
intersecting each prefix with the original singleton could recover the
same support, but would describe a different sequence of operations.
Here creation of sibling states precedes descending to state 9, so DFS
emits 0,5,9,6,7,... rather than simply walking the state vector.

> Check exact work families and the output barrier

For N identical baskets containing all U items, every nonempty subset is
frequent whenever 1<=minimum support<=N. There are F=2^U−1 outputs.
Each nonsingleton is formed by exactly one intersection, so R=F−U.
Both operand tidsets contain every row. Thus merge steps and matched
tids both equal N·R, and peak DFS frames equal U. Explicit frames avoid
call-stack recursion; they cannot avoid exponential output.

For U disjoint singleton baskets at threshold one, only U singleton
outputs survive. All U(U−1)/2 root pairs are nevertheless attempted and
fail, with one merge step each and no matched tids. The peak frame count
is one. The number of outputs alone therefore does not determine work.
The families below have different row counts (five versus U); the
comparison checks these formulas, rather than claiming a speed ranking.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/eclat_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double>x,dense_outputs,dense_attempts,sparse_attempts;
  std::print("| U | dense F | dense R | dense steps | dense frames | disjoint F | disjoint R | disjoint steps |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t u:{2,4,6,8,10,12}){
    std::vector<std::vector<std::size_t>> dense(5,std::vector<std::size_t>(u)),disjoint(u);
    for(auto& row:dense)std::iota(row.begin(),row.end(),0);for(std::size_t i=0;i<u;++i)disjoint[i]={i};
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::eclat_frequent_itemsets_work(dense,5),b=dm::algorithms::eclat_frequent_itemsets_work(disjoint,1);
    const auto f=(std::size_t{1}<<u)-1,r=f-u,pairs=u*(u-1)/2;
    if(a.itemsets.size()!=f||a.work.intersections!=r||a.work.intersection_steps!=5*r||a.work.matched_tids!=5*r||a.work.peak_frames!=u||b.itemsets.size()!=u||b.work.intersections!=pairs||b.work.intersection_steps!=pairs||b.work.matched_tids!=0||b.work.peak_frames!=1)throw std::runtime_error("work identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",u,f,r,a.work.intersection_steps,a.work.peak_frames,b.itemsets.size(),b.work.intersections,b.work.intersection_steps);
    x.push_back(u);dense_outputs.push_back(std::log2(f+1));dense_attempts.push_back(std::log2(r+1));sparse_attempts.push_back(std::log2(pairs+1));
  }
  std::print("\n| identical rows N, U=6 | intersections | merge steps | matched tids |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{1,2,4,8,16}){std::vector<std::vector<std::size_t>> tx(n,{0,1,2,3,4,5});const auto r=dm::algorithms::eclat_frequent_itemsets_work(tx,n);
    if(r.work.intersections!=57||r.work.intersection_steps!=57*n||r.work.matched_tids!=57*n)throw std::runtime_error("row identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,r.work.intersections,r.work.intersection_steps,r.work.matched_tids);}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,dense_outputs,"F+1",{37,99,235}).points(x,dense_outputs,"",{37,99,235},5).title("Dense output: log2(F+1) equals U").x_label("Observed items U").y_label("log2(count)").y_limits(0,14);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,dense_attempts,"dense R+1",{220,38,38}).points(x,dense_attempts,"",{220,38,38},5).line(x,sparse_attempts,"disjoint R+1",{22,163,74}).points(x,sparse_attempts,"",{22,163,74},5).title("Attempted intersections include failures").x_label("Observed items U").y_label("log2(R+1)").y_limits(0,14);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,520).title("Measured logical work, with exact family checks").fit_panels().save_svg("build/eclat_work.svg");
}
