// result_end
\caption(All item-count and row-count sweeps satisfy the exact formulas. Dense output is exponential; even disjoint data has quadratic failed root attempts.)
\alttext(Two native plots show the linear log2 dense output count and compare exponential dense intersection counts with quadratic disjoint failed attempts.)

For raw row lengths b_i, normalization sorts and deduplicates each row,
costing O(sum b_i log(b_i+1)); constructing the ordered item map adds
O(E log(U+1)) for E unique row-item incidences. The tidset kernel costs
O(sum over attempts (|L|+|R|)), bounded by O(RN). Prefix construction
and output are additional, as is final canonical sorting, bounded by
O(F log(F+1)·U) item comparisons. Each emitted set may try at most U
later siblings, so R<=UF; this loose bound includes failed candidates.

Input normalization and the root vertical index require O(N+E) storage.
Conditional tidsets across live frames can retain O(U²N) row ids, plus
prefix/candidate metadata, and output stores sum over frequent X of |X|
item ids. This plain sorted-list implementation uses neither diffsets,
bitmap compression nor support-based item reordering. The experiments
measure neither wall time nor the relative performance of other miners.

> Mine canonical Titanic passenger baskets

Use all 891 rows of dm::datasets::titanic(), selecting Pclass, Sex and
Survived. encode_transactions() gives one item per non-null selected cell,
with stable labels such as Sex=female. All three selected columns are
complete here: 2,673 incidences, seven observed items. The support floor
is 45 passengers, about 5.05% of 891. Three mutually exclusive columns
make no transaction longer than three, so no nonzero-support four-item
set can occur. The table prints every frequent set rather than selecting
only a favourable association.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/eclat_titanic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto encoded=dm::algorithms::encode_transactions(dm::datasets::titanic(),{"Pclass","Sex","Survived"});
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::eclat_trace(encoded.transactions,45);
  const auto as_map=[](const auto& sets){std::map<std::vector<std::size_t>,std::size_t> out;for(const auto& s:sets)out.emplace(s.items,s.support);return out;};
  const bool apriori=as_map(t.itemsets)==as_map(dm::algorithms::apriori_frequent_itemsets(encoded.transactions,45));
  const bool fp=as_map(t.itemsets)==as_map(dm::algorithms::fp_growth_frequent_itemsets(encoded.transactions,45));
  if(t.work.transactions!=891||t.work.raw_items!=2673||t.singleton_count!=7||!apriori||!fp)throw std::runtime_error("dataset evidence changed");
  std::print("Titanic: {} rows; {} raw items; {} unique incidences; {} observed items; minimum support 45.\n",t.work.transactions,t.work.raw_items,t.work.incidences,t.singleton_count);
  std::print("{} frequent sets; {} intersections; {} merge steps; {} matched tids; {} peak frames. Apriori agrees {}; FP-growth agrees {}.\n\n",t.itemsets.size(),t.work.intersections,t.work.intersection_steps,t.work.matched_tids,t.work.peak_frames,apriori,fp);
  std::print("| frequent passenger itemset | support | share of 891 |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::vector<double> sizes(3),singleton_supports;std::vector<std::string> singleton_labels;
  for(const auto& f:t.itemsets){std::print("| {} | {} | {:.4f} |\n",dm::algorithms::itemset_label(f.items,encoded.labels),f.support,double(f.support)/891);sizes.at(f.items.size()-1)++;}
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.singleton_count;++i){const auto& s=t.states[i];singleton_labels.push_back(encoded.labels.at(s.itemset.items[0]));singleton_supports.push_back(s.itemset.support);}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(singleton_supports,singleton_labels,"",{37,99,235}).title("Selected passenger attributes").x_label("Observed item").y_label("Support count").y_limits(0,700);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(sizes,std::vector<std::string>{"1 item","2 items","3 items"},"",{22,163,74}).title("Frequent sets by cardinality").x_label("Itemset size").y_label("Number of frequent sets").y_limits(0,20);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,1).add(a).add(b).size(1000,850).title("Titanic: Pclass, Sex and Survived, minimum support 45").fit_panels().save_svg("build/eclat_titanic.svg");
}
